      "question_type": "LONG",
      "stem_text": "The point $P = (-1,0)$ lies on the ellipse $4 x^2 + y^2 = 4.$ Let $Q$ be another point on\nthis ellipse, and let $d$ be the maximum length of $\\overline{PQ}.$ Find $d^2.$",
      "options": null,
      "marks": 10,
      "gold_answer": "Let $Q = (x,y).$ From the given information, $y^2 = 4 - 4 x^2.$ Therefore, \\begin{align*}\nPQ^2 &= (x + 1)^2 + y^2 \\\\ &= x^2 + 2 x + 1 + 4 - 4 x^2 \\\\ &= -3 x^2 + 2 x + 5 \\\\ &= -3\n\\left( x - \\frac{1}{3} \\right)^2 + \\frac{16}{3}. \\end{align*}This is maximized when $x =\n\\frac{1}{3},$ and $d^2 = \\boxed{\\frac{16}{3}}.$",
